      "severity": "Critical",
      "reproduction_evidence": "Coursework weight sum = 0.0%; Exam submissions = 0.",
      "root_cause": "Module GGG utilizes a 100% formative continuous coursework design (all 9 assessments have weight=0.0%). The final exam carries 100% of the course grade but is completely unobserved in studentAssessment.csv. The model is forced to train on non-determinative practice exercises where passing or failing carries zero course stakes.",
      "impact": "Decouples assessment failure risk from actual course completion and module passing.",
      "proposed_remediation": "Document curricular anomaly in governance policy. Flag GGG continuous coursework as formative-only. Exclude unweighted CMAs from high-stakes intervention triggers."
    },
    {
      "failure_id": "FAIL-GGG-02",
      "component": "Temporal Feature Pipeline (`src/temporal_feature_engineering.py`)",
      "severity": "High",
      "reproduction_evidence": "82.18% of CMAs (7856/9559) submitted prior to cutoff Day 222 (mean early = 54.06 days).",
      "root_cause": "All 6 CMAs in GGG share an identical end-of-term nominal scheduled deadline (Day 229 / 222). In reality, they are self-paced quizzes submitted throughout the term (median 47 days before cutoff). Evaluating them at Day 222 uses telemetry generated weeks after submission, creating chronological inversion.",
      "impact": "Decouples student portal study activity from assessment performance, yielding false-positive alerts on students who completed coursework early.",
      "proposed_remediation": "For self-paced quizzes, nominal terminal deadlines should not be treated as fixed synchronous milestones. Establish a Low-Confidence Advisory Protocol for GGG CMAs."
    },
    {
      "failure_id": "FAIL-GGG-03",
      "component": "Feature Engineering Logic (`num_previous_scheduled_assessments`)",
      "severity": "Medium",
      "reproduction_evidence": "Values assigned to clustered CMAs: [3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8].",
      "root_cause": "Feature logic assigns arbitrary loop index k from enumerate(cohort_sched.iterrows()). When 6 CMAs share the exact same scheduled date (Day 229), they receive arbitrary integers 3 to 8 based on file row order.",
      "impact": "Injects artificial, arbitrary numerical feature noise into model splits.",
      "proposed_remediation": "Compute num_previous_scheduled_assessments as the count of assessments with strictly smaller scheduled_date (cohort_sched['scheduled_date'] < current_date).count(), ensuring tied dates share the exact same integer."
    },
    {
      "failure_id": "FAIL-GGG-04",
      "component": "Feature Engineering Logic (`prior_subs` strictly smaller scheduled_date filter)",
      "severity": "Medium",
      "reproduction_evidence": "Max prior scored assessments in CMAs = 3 (exactly the 3 TMAs).",
      "root_cause": "Filter condition (cohort_subs['scheduled_date'] < a_date) excludes all peer CMAs sharing the same scheduled date (229 < 229 is False), even when a student completed peer CMAs months prior.",
      "impact": "Information loss: Model is blind to prior completed CMAs when predicting subsequent CMAs.",
      "proposed_remediation": "Filter prior submissions by submission and grading timestamp (date_submitted + delay <= cutoff_t) rather than scheduled date strictly."
